==Finnish==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ru|fi}} {{term|гласность||openness|tr=glasnost|sc=Cyrl}}
The root of the word "glasnost" is "glas" ("глас") which is an Old Russian word for "voice" ("голос"). Therefore, "glasnost" literally translates as "open voice", meaning a COMPLETE public exposure of any given issue (enabling anyone who is interested to have a full access to information). It is also worth mentioning that "glasnost" is an active process with the main purpose of making an EFFORT (by those who were then in power) to inform the public rather than making information simply available to the public.

